language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ packing_rectangles: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Place a set of rectangles, each with a given width and height, inside a larger rectangle so that no two
$ rectangles overlap and every rectangle lies within the larger one. The rectangles are not rotated. Minimise the area
$ of the larger rectangle needed to pack all of them.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `packing_rectangles.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/packing_rectangles.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `packing_rectangles_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py packing_rectangles.json
$   savilerow model.eprime packing_rectangles_1.param -run-solver

$ widths_dim1: the number of rectangles (derived from the data)
given widths_dim1 : int
$ heights_dim1: the same number of rectangles (derived from the data)
given heights_dim1 : int
$ widths[i]: the width of rectangle i (indices from 1)
given widths : matrix indexed by [int(1..widths_dim1)] of int(1..)
$ heights[i]: the height of rectangle i (indices from 1)
given heights : matrix indexed by [int(1..heights_dim1)] of int(1..)

$ the sum of all widths and the sum of all heights: the enclosing rectangle never needs to be larger
letting sum_widths = sum i : int(1..widths_dim1) . widths[i]
letting sum_heights = sum i : int(1..heights_dim1) . heights[i]

$ pos_x[i]: the x coordinate of the left edge of rectangle i, counted from 0 (indices from 1)
find pos_x : matrix indexed by [int(1..widths_dim1)] of int(0..sum_widths)
$ pos_y[i]: the y coordinate of the bottom edge of rectangle i, counted from 0 (indices from 1)
find pos_y : matrix indexed by [int(1..widths_dim1)] of int(0..sum_heights)
$ total_x: the width of the enclosing rectangle
find total_x : int(1..sum_widths)
$ total_y: the height of the enclosing rectangle
find total_y : int(1..sum_heights)

minimising total_x * total_y
such that
$ every rectangle lies within the enclosing rectangle
forAll i : int(1..widths_dim1) . (pos_x[i] + widths[i] <= total_x /\ pos_y[i] + heights[i] <= total_y),
$ no two rectangles overlap: for each pair, one lies to the left of, right of, below or above the other
forAll i : int(1..widths_dim1) . forAll j : int(i+1..widths_dim1) . (pos_x[i] + widths[i] <= pos_x[j] \/ pos_x[j] + widths[j] <= pos_x[i] \/ pos_y[i] + heights[i] <= pos_y[j] \/ pos_y[j] + heights[j] <= pos_y[i])
